messages.text:
The reviewer approved the #10021 plan with four amendments:
- an integration assertion that the constructor call keeps its three reasons while the receiver's type becomes Complete;
- one Scala control, if an existing fixture has one;
- existing or minimal controls for anonymous creations, incomplete or ambiguous qualifiers, and owner mismatches;
- a note in the PR about where the three reasons come from.

Identity is allocated: ICFG full v710 / read v709, plus the policy token `-10021-creation-type-from-qualifier`. I'll start the branch from current master and make the code and identity changes myself, since they are small and settled. A child then does the tests and validation.

Both rulings are in:
- **#10021 is accepted.** Amendment 1 moves to `java-indexed-import-destinations`. The PR will explain why the #7618 golden doesn't move, and the fully qualified form is left to #7804. The declared-local asymmetry gets its own follow-up issue.
- **#7708 is approved with amendments:**
  - keep the read-side traversal;
  - follow exact-type links only, declared through a Java language hook in the shared builder;
  - stay `Leaf` when sources disagree or a path is incomplete;
  - return Inapplicable only on exact provenance and a conclusive widening;
  - add extra tests, including the poly case, wildcard actuals and a Go regression check.

  Identity is allocated: ICFG v711/v710, plus the token `-7708-declared-type-argument-transport`.

I'll start the #10021 completion first; it is ready on its branch.
